# Updating translations

## gettext (`.po`)

- **msgid-copy is not a translation** — except **keep-English** packaging field /
  code-snippet literals (e.g. `Architecture: all`, `Source=%s`, multi-line
  `%build` / Makefile examples) that zh_CN/zh_TW also leave in English. Empty
  `msgstr` or a prose msgid-copy (where a primary locale translated the same
  msgid) counts as untranslated / omitted. English variants `en_GB` / `en_AU` /
  … may keep `msgstr == msgid` when msgid is English.
- **≤20% completion** ⇒ treat the catalog as missing. Rewrite the whole `.po` by hand.
  Do **not** write patch/sed/Python scripts to “fix” a mostly-empty catalog.
- **Incremental updates** (a few new msgids): translate them yourself, then batch-apply
  with **`poedit`** — usually no other tooling is needed:

```bash
poedit -l ab,de,fg <<EOT
<msgid>	<ab>	<de>	<fg>
<msgid>	<ab>	<de>	<fg>
EOT
```

  Tabs separate fields. Do not feed poedit msgid copies or placeholders.

## README / man (AsciiDoc)

- Whole-document locale files under `man/<locale>/`. Prefer hand translation.
- **`googletranslator`** can help for long adoc/README text — use the local
  HTTP proxy (`http://localhost:8118`; see **proxy.mdc**). **Do not** use Google
  Translate for gettext catalogs.
